  "instance_name": "camping",
  "label": "Gaming term: Camping",
  "description": "In video games, particularly first-person shooters like Call of Duty, 'camping' refers to a gameplay tactic where a player remains stationary in one location, often with a weapon aimed outward, to ambush or attack opponents who pass by. It is often seen as a defensive or aggressive strategy, and the term is used humorously here to imply the player is already deeply engaged in this behavior when a new game is released.",
